# 57: a recursive list spread CONJOINED WITH A MAP did not terminate
# at depth two, in BOTH ports. FIXED 2026-10-09 (BUGS.md §57): a list's
# spread meets each element once, so it answers at once in both.
#
# run: node ../../../ts/bin/aontu.js recursive-spread-conjunct-hangs.aontu
# run: aontu-go recursive-spread-conjunct-hangs.aontu
#
# expected: {"d":{"kids":[{"kids":[{"name":"c"}],"name":"b"}],"name":"a"}}
# actual (both ports): as expected
#
# Before the fix it allocated without bound inside one fixpoint pass
# (563 MB at 21 s, 700 MB at 41 s in TypeScript), where the pass budget
# does not reach, until the depth budget refused it as unify_cycle far
# past any practical wait. Pinned by the rows under "A spread meets an
# element once" in test/spec/recursion.tsv.
%T = {name: string, kids?: [&: %T & {}]}
d: %T & {name: a, kids: [{name: b, kids: [{name: c}]}]}
